                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Nelson, Bert N./2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-16T12:00:00+08:00">October 16,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 16—5:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>907. Hankow’s October 14, 5 p.m. The Legation is telegraphing Adams to take this
                    matter up at once with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs with a view to effecting
                    the release of the Reverend Nelson at the earliest possible moment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
